      "writtenOn": "2023-08-17T00:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is what we do in the Skia Infrastructure repository: https://skia.googlesource.com/buildbot/+/f1d21dc58818cd6aba0a7822e59d37636aefe936/WORKSPACE#391\n\nThe `git config --system` commands do not affect the developer\u0027s environment; they only affect the \"system-wide\" `gitconfig` file, which per `man git-config` refers to `$(prefix)/etc/gitconfig`. It\u0027s unclear to me what `$(prefix)` means. Some folks on Stack Overflow say it\u0027s a setting determined at build time. Regardless, in practice it resolves correctly:\n\n```\n$ cat $(bazel info output_base)/external/git_linux_amd64/etc/gitconfig\n[user]\n        name \u003d Bazel Test User\n        email \u003d bazel-test-user@example.com\n```\n\nThe above snippet should produce the same result on both the Buildbot and Skia repositories.\n\nNote that the Bazel-downloaded `git` binary should only be visible to those Bazel targets that add `@git_linux_amd64//:all_files` as a `data` dependency.",
      "parentUuid": "c817ccc0_923bb27d",
