    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "044f1021_3176c215",
        "filename": "infra/bots/gen_tasks_logic/gen_tasks_logic.go",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2154,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-17T00:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about it but went this route because `test_suite` does not allow wildcard expressions. This means if someone casually adds a Go test and forgets to add it to the `test_suite`, it won\u0027t be covered by this task.\n\nIdeally, we would want to use a single label or wildcard, presumably `//...`, and have `cpu_tests.go` (or a new `go_tests.go` task driver) limit `//...` to only `go_test` targets (e.g. via `bazel query \u0027kind(go_test, //...)\u0027` once we fix the issues mentioned in the above comments).\n\nDid you still want me to go the `test_suite` route? Any other thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "a473b332_0a88743f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2154,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2154,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "802523ec5865c0418f09f51386cb1bcd93d2854a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20312410_92a760a6",
