      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T18:17:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, using a `test_suite` for now.\n\nFWIW, we use wildcards elsewhere. For example in the Buildbot repo we `bazel test //... --config\u003dremote`. Requiring folks to add tests to known test suites might lead to omission errors. This is fine in the short term, but I believe we should aspire to make wildcards work in the long run.\n\nSome ideas:\n\n- Leverage the `target_compatible_with` attribute in tests (https://bazel.build/extending/platforms#skipping-incompatible-targets)\n\n- Filter tests by tag, for example `bazel test //... --test_tag_filters\u003dsometag` (https://bazel.build/reference/command-line-reference#flag--test_tag_filters). This could be a good solution for Go tests because as mentioned in https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12618, today we cannot tell Bazel to only run `go_test` targets. It is possible to tell Gazelle to add a specific tag to all `go_test` targets it produces.",
      "parentUuid": "20312410_92a760a6",
